,"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":18,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"numerical_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"ok\",\"summary\":\"The paper's reported counts, shares and percentages mostly reconcile with the page text, the retained table and figure crops, and the page images. Table 3/4 cells, the 97% agreement, Table 6 totals, the Table 8 listing shares, and the Figure 2, 3 and 4 labels all check. Three defects remain. (1) The pilot-yield sentence divides a count of distinct openings (2) by a count of articles (34) and reports 'about 6 percent'; the paper's own counts give 5 relevant articles (14.7%) or 3 after excluding pre-opening articles (8.8%). (2) Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 shows the second coder coded the Stord article relevant. (3) The 96-article and 44-project totals add four pilot articles and one project to the rounds 2-4 totals, but the overlap between the pilot and rounds 2-4 is not stated, so these totals cannot be verified. Structured table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, per the parser-quality guidance.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"NUM-001\",\"category\":\"denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The pilot-yield sentence reports 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)' as concerning an opening that took place, but 2 is the count of distinct openings (projects), not articles. The paper's own counts give 5 relevant articles, or 3 once the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Figure 1 labels '2' as 'Distinct openings that took place' and '5' as articles coded relevant. Section 3.1.4 says the five relevant articles cover two unique openings (four on Homborsund, one on Stod), and that two Homborsund articles were published before the opening, leaving three relevant articles in the validation. The numerator in the 6% figure is therefore a project count and the denominator an article count. Using article counts throughout, 5/34 = 14.7% (matching the '15 % retained' label in Figure 1) or 3/34 = 8.8% if the pre-opening articles are excluded. The sentence is also the abstract-level motivation ('keyword search alone is too noisy'); the low-yield conclusion survives either denominator, but the stated 6% does not describe articles. The Figure 1 caption makes the same mismatch ('Only 2 of 70 search hits').\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 1 labels also checked against the page-4 image: 70, 34 (49 % retained), 5 (15 % retained), 2 distinct openings.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"This resulted in five relevant articles, eight unclear and 21 not relevant.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Same paragraph states 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.'\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 unique articles concern an opening that took place\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Five articles were coded relevant and concern the two openings; 2 counts projects.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"6\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"percent of unique articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Reported share 'about 6 percent' computed from 2 of 34\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.5\",\"scale\":\"percent\"},{\"value\":\"5\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Articles coded relevant in manual coding (5/34 = 14.7%)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"distinct openings\",\"sample\":\"pilot sample\",\"denominator\":\"not an article count\",\"context\":\"Distinct openings that took place; the numerator used in the 6% figure\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"The numerator in the reported share counts distinct openings (projects) and the denominator counts articles, so the share does not describe articles. An article-based share uses the same denominator of 34 articles.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Reported about 6% (2/34). Article-based alternatives from the paper's own counts are 5/34 = 14.7% (all articles coded relevant) or 3/34 = 8.8% (excluding the two pre-opening Homborsund articles).\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The authors may have intended a project-level yield (2 openings out of 34 articles) and described it as an article share.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State which unit is meant. For an article-level yield, give the number of articles concerning an opening that took place, 5 or 3, and the matching percentage. Otherwise label the 2/34 as openings per unique article.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Rewrite the sentence and the Figure 1 caption so that the numerator and denominator use the same unit, either articles or projects, and report the matching percentage.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-002\",\"category\":\"cross_source_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 states that the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 and Section 4.1 show the second coder coded the Stord article relevant (the single disagreement), so only the pilot coder coded it not relevant.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses of the Articles, footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"The Stord project appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 3 has the pilot coder as rows and the second coder as columns. The 'Not relevant' pilot row has 1 in the 'Relevant' second-coder column, and the second coder's relevant total is 4 versus 3 for the pilot coder. Section 4.1 says the coders disagree on one article, the Stord dispute, and Section 4.2 says the LLM majority (2 of 3 runs) coded the same article relevant. Footnote 3 therefore conflicts with the retained counts. The page-10 footnote marker is attached to the word 'The' in the extracted text; the quote starts after it.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6, footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break in the extraction; the footnote marker attached to 'The' is not part of the quote.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text (Table 3 and Section 4.1)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1 / Table 3\",\"text_quote\":\"Not relevant 1 30 31\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Row read from page text, not the structured CSV, because of the parser-quality warning on header merging. Text also says 'The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County'.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord coded not relevant by both human coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 shows one article coded relevant by the second coder only; Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord article.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"1\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Table 3 cell: pilot coder not relevant, second coder relevant (the Stord article)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Table 3 total coded relevant by the second coder, versus 3 for the pilot coder\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"human coders (claimed)\",\"sample\":\"two human coders\",\"denominator\":\"2 coders\",\"context\":\"Footnote 3 says 'both human coders' coded the Stord project not relevant\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Same 34-article pilot sample and same relevance variable; footnote 3 refers to the same Stord article that Section 4.1 describes as the only disagreement between the two coders.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Footnote 3 implies 0 of 2 coders coded the Stord article relevant; Table 3 implies 1 of 2 coders (the second coder), plus the LLM majority.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The footnote may be meant to say 'by the pilot coder' or may refer to a different Stord article.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Reconcile the footnote with Table 3 and Section 4.1 and state which coder or coders coded the Stord article not relevant.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Correct footnote 3 to match Table 3, or clarify that it refers to a different article. Also check that the 44-project and 96-article totals correctly include this article.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-003\",\"category\":\"aggregation_unspecified\",\"finding_summary\":\"The totals of 96 article records and 44 projects add four pilot articles and one Stord project to the 92 articles and 43 projects from rounds 2-4, but the paper does not say whether the pilot articles and projects (Homborsund, Gusthaugen-Leinskorsen) overlap with rounds 2-4, so the 96 and 44 totals cannot be verified.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"low\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses of the Articles, footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44 unique projects.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The paper does not state whether the pilot articles (2 September to 10 October 2026) overlap with rounds 2-4 (October 2025 to October 2026), or which of the 43 projects the pilot Homborsund and Gusthaugen-Leinskorsen openings belong to. Without that, whether 92 + 4 = 96 and 43 + 1 = 44 avoid double counting cannot be checked.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Footnote 3 defines 96 = 92 + 4 pilot articles and 44 = 43 + the Stord project, said to appear only in the pilot. Table 4 shows 4 LLM-relevant pilot articles, which matches the four. Rounds 2-4 span October 2025 to October 2026 and the pilot sample runs 2 September to 10 October 2026, so the date ranges overlap. The 44 total also requires the pilot's Homborsund and Gusthaugen projects to be among the 43; the Table 7 note refers to rounds 1-4. Section 6.3 gives 17 + 2 = 19 day-dated projects out of 44, equal to Table 6's 19 day-dated projects out of 43, which is consistent only if the Stord project is not day-dated. The abstract and Section 7 consistently use 92 and 43.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6, footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote begins after the footnote marker '3' attached to 'The' in the extraction.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 9 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md\",\"page\":9,\"page_label\":\"9\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM coded 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4, published between October 2025 and October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Date range overlaps the pilot period.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Pilot period.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"96 article records and 44 unique projects across the pilot and later rounds\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"cannot_verify\",\"note\":\"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2-4 is not stated.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Does 96 = 92 + 4 and 44 = 43 + 1 count each article and project once, given that the pilot period falls inside the rounds 2-4 date range?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"96\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"article records\",\"sample\":\"pilot plus rounds 2-4\",\"denominator\":\"not applicable\",\"context\":\"Total article records reporting an opening\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"92\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"rounds 2-4\",\"denominator\":\"3,187 articles coded\",\"context\":\"Relevant articles in rounds 2-4\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"44\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"projects\",\"sample\":\"pilot plus rounds 2-4\",\"denominator\":\"not applicable\",\"context\":\"Unique projects, equal to 43 plus the Stord project\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Whether pilot articles are included in the 3,187 articles of rounds 2-4\",\"Which of the 43 projects correspond to the pilot's Homborsund and Gusthaugen-Leinskorsen openings\",\"How many pilot articles per project are added to the 92\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State how the pilot and rounds 2-4 were combined and de-duplicated, and list which projects the four pilot articles belong to.\"}],\"notes\":[\"Structured table CSV/markdown were not used as primary evidence, per the parser-quality warnings. Values were read from page text, with Figure 1, Figure 2, Figure 3 and Figure 4 compared against the page-4, page-16 and page-17 images.\",\"Recomputed with no discrepancy: 70 - 36 = 34; 5 + 8 + 21 = 34; Table 2 article count